# Line endings are part of this artifact's integrity, not a style preference.
#
# `core.autocrlf=true` is set machine-wide on the machine this was built on, which means a
# fresh checkout would rewrite every LF to CRLF -- and then `MANIFEST.sha256` (computed over
# LF bytes) would fail for every file, and the raw traces would no longer be the bytes the
# analysis scripts were run against. The rules below make a checkout byte-identical on every
# platform, which is what "reproducible" has to mean for an evidence repository.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Evidence and its digest are opaque bytes: never normalise, never convert.
runs/** -text
MANIFEST.sha256 -text
